WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.420
Film Courage: How do you know that the director
is the real deal? Brad Rushing, Cinematographer:

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:10.599
I'm not especially big on judging people in
an absolute way so what I would characterize

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:20.490
is directors I am most fulfilled working with
and that would be interactive ones. You know

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:30.740
I want somebody who both brings ideas and
has very strong feelings but is also collaborative

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:37.050
and is willing to if a better idea is presented,
whether it's the producer or the actor or

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:44.000
the craft services person, is open to considering
that because it's about the movie we are all

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:57.079
making not about their ego. So that's my preferred
archetype. The ones who aren't prepared frustrate

00:00:57.079 --> 00:01:07.250
me because we should all be prepared. The
ones who when I say how would you like to

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:13.120
shoot this? And they say What do you think?
A few times, that's okay. I mean I've asked

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.920
my lighting crew before I'm a little stymied
do you have any ideas but but if that is the

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:25.422
standard mo well i'm carrying them and it's
it's not fun for me i mean maybe it would

00:01:25.422 --> 00:01:30.050
be fun for somebody else maybe there's you
know a dp out there who just has delusions

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:35.470
of grandeur and as a wannabe director who
would be thrilled to work with that person

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:42.060
but for me um it's a collaboration you know
i want to feel like we're we're doing something

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:47.040
together and if i'm getting nothing from them
then it's kind of like it's just not that

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:55.610
much fun and same on the other hand if i have
somebody who is really overbearing and controlling

00:01:55.610 --> 00:02:02.110
and i feel like i have no input then i just
you know i don't it's not fun it's not exciting

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:09.710
it's kind of like i just feel like i'm um
you know just a i don't even know what you'd

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:18.150
call it just a um a worker drone you know
just taking instructions and not not interpreting

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:23.780
at all so you know again to me the sweet spot
is in the middle and there's a range too i

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.720
mean you know it could be you know a little
more me or a little more of them i mean that's

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:33.010
okay you know it could tilt and and you know
with with good people sometimes it does tilt

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:37.230
you know sometimes you know like i said you
know sometimes you know somebody may say to

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:41.480
me why don't you take the lead on this one
i'm like okay let's do that you know or sometimes

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:47.970
they're like no i know exactly how i want
this um so so you know that dynamic being

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:53.370
being flexible and throughout that's okay
but it's it's really that when you get in

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:58.710
that default mode if it tilts too far one
way or the other and just every day is like

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:03.870
that then you know it's that's not the thing
that gets me excited to get out of bed in

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:13.030
the morning what is not being prepared um
well not having a sense of how you want to

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:20.739
cover a scene not having a sense of of the
type of coverage you want not having some

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:27.599
